// STATUS: historical_record — consumido por fuse fuente THEORY-02 (vos_proofs.vsm:7 — fuse 8 sources); contenido canonical en vos_proofs.vsm · archivo 2026-08-15
// (THEORY-FUSE-REMAINDER censo; contenido en el target canonical, este doc es fuente histórica.)
// composition_proof.vsm — THEORY-COMP — compositional viability under ψ-coupling
// domain_context: {target=vos_kernel, env=theory, layer=L+2}
// origin: dynamics_choice.vsm §G3 (FULLY_CLOSED) — formalization of the 3 no-compose
//         corollaries + the positive composition theorem.
// status: derivable from Ax_SplitOperator + Ax_ψ_Preserve + Ax_RecurrentSet + Def_ArbiterAPI
// implements: the proof obligations behind projects/vsf-nucleus/src/coupling.rs (F5.x.6)
//
// NOTATION
//   V_A, V_B          viable systems (each an ℝ¹²⁸ kernel with its own Ω, S3, trust)
//   ⊗_ψ               ψ-composition (coupling.rs::couple) producing the joint system V_AB
//   viable(V)         V is positive-recurrent on a compact R ⊂ Ω (Ax_RecurrentSet)
//   J_ψ               Jacobian of the coupling map ψ (M_ψ = U·Vᵀ, rank ≤ 16; coupling.rs)
//   B_h               hardware resource ceiling (A3 budget); B_AB joint budget
//   S3_AB             a shared controller/arbiter for the joint system (Def_ArbiterAPI)


// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// POSITIVE RESULT — when composition preserves viability
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

theorem(Thm_Compose, "ψ-composition preserves viability under 4 preconditions"):
  statement:
    "viable(V_A) ∧ viable(V_B)
       ∧ (P1) ∃ S3_AB                              // a joint arbiter exists
       ∧ (P2) Σ_i quota_i ≤ B_AB ≤ B_h             // budgets fit the hardware ceiling
       ∧ (P3) ‖J_ψ‖ < 1                            // coupling is contractive
       ∧ (P4) trust_AB ≥ min(trust_A, trust_B)     // Ax_ψ_Preserve trust clause
     ⇒ viable(V_AB)."

  proof(Thm_Compose):
    step_1_state_space:
      "By Ax_ψ_Preserve (coupling.rs), ψ(x_A,x_B) ∈ Ω_AB ⇔ x_A∈Ω_A ∧ x_B∈Ω_B ∧ (P4).
       Inputs are viable ⇒ x_A∈R_A⊂Ω_A, x_B∈R_B⊂Ω_B ⇒ joint state ∈ Ω_AB. (P4) closes the
       trust clause. So the joint operator maps Ω_AB → Ω_AB (well-posed)."
    step_2_lyapunov_composite:
      "Define L_AB = L_A∘π_A + L_B∘π_B + κ·‖coupling residual‖. Each L_i satisfies
       Thm_DirectExpansion (lyapunov_proof.vsm) on its own recurrent set. The cross term
       is controlled by the coupling Jacobian J_ψ."
    step_3_contraction:
      "(P3) ‖J_ψ‖ < 1 ⇒ the coupling is a contraction in the joint metric ⇒ the cross term
       cannot inject net variety: E[ΔL_AB] ≤ E[ΔL_A] + E[ΔL_B] + (‖J_ψ‖−1)·‖residual‖ ≤ 0
       outside the joint recurrent set R_AB. (Banach-style: contraction + two recurrent
       summands ⇒ a joint recurrent set exists.)"
    step_4_budget:
      "(P2) Σ quota_i ≤ B_h ⇒ no resource starvation ⇒ each V_i keeps the budget headroom
       its own viability proof assumed (A3). (P1) S3_AB enforces the allocation."
    conclude:
      "P1..P4 ⇒ ∃ compact R_AB ⊂ Ω_AB positive-recurrent ⇒ viable(V_AB). ∎"

  remark:
    "The four preconditions are exactly the four no-compose failure modes negated.
     Each corollary below is the contrapositive of one precondition."


// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// FAILURE COROLLARIES — when composition destroys viability
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

corollary(Cor_NoCompose_1, "resource contention"):
  statement:  "Σ_i quota_i > B_h  ⇒  ¬viable(⊗_ψ V_i)."
  negates:    "P2 (budget fits)."
  proof:
    "If aggregate demand exceeds the hardware ceiling, ∃ V_j whose realized budget
     B_realized(V_j) < B_assumed(V_j). The γ-term of L (γ·max(0, B−B_avail),
     lyapunov_proof.vsm) becomes persistently positive for V_j ⇒ E[ΔL_j] > 0 sustained
     ⇒ V_j leaves its recurrent set ⇒ ¬viable(V_j) ⇒ ¬viable(⊗_ψ V_i). ∎"
  enforcement: "Def_ArbiterAPI.allocate must reject Σ quota > B_h (admission control)."

corollary(Cor_NoCompose_2, "algedonic resonance"):
  statement:  "∃ loop φ↑_A→B→A with loop_gain > 1  ⇒  ¬viable(⊗_ψ V_i)."
  negates:    "P3 (‖J_ψ‖ < 1) — a feedback loop with gain > 1 makes the coupling expansive."
  proof:
    "An algedonic/φ↑ cycle A→B→A with gain g multiplies a perturbation by gⁿ after n
     traversals. g > 1 ⇒ unbounded amplification ⇒ ‖J_ψ‖ ≥ g > 1 ⇒ Thm_Compose step_3
     fails ⇒ E[ΔL_AB] > 0 ⇒ joint state diverges (Regime::Diverging, lyapunov.rs). ∎"
  enforcement:
    "coupling.rs keeps M_ψ = U·Vᵀ low-rank with bounded singular values; a runtime
     ‖J_ψ‖ check (largest singular value < 1) gates the coupling. Algedonic ALG-1 decay
     (invariant_checker.rs) independently caps cascade gain."

corollary(Cor_NoCompose_3, "phase aliasing"):
  statement_ideal:
    "Δt_A / Δt_B ∉ ℚ  ∧  no sync protocol  ⇒  ¬viable(⊗_ψ V_i)."
  statement_pragmatic:   // all real Δt are floats (rational); use a tolerance
    "|Δt_A − Δt_B| > tol  ∧  no sync  ⇒  aliasing risk ⇒ ¬viable(⊗_ψ V_i)."
  negates:    "the implicit synchrony Thm_Compose assumes when summing E[ΔL_A]+E[ΔL_B]."
  proof:
    "If the two kernels tick at incommensurable rates with no synchronization, a σ_i
     measured by one is stale when used by the other beyond Bound_Staleness
     (adaptive_clock.rs): |σ(t₁)−σ(t₀)| > 2·Λ·Δt_max ⇒ the staleness Lyapunov violation
     ½‖∇²L‖(2ΛΔt)² is no longer ≤ ε ⇒ the descent bound breaks ⇒ no joint recurrent set. ∎"
  enforcement:
    "adaptive_clock.rs SeqLock σ_global + Bound_Staleness gives the sync protocol:
     bound Δt_max ≤ √(ε/‖∇²L‖)/Λ on BOTH sides ⇒ aliasing controlled."

corollary(Cor_4, "trust mismatch", proposed=Claude):
  statement:  "|trust_A − trust_B| > τ_threshold  ⇒  revisit ψ.handshake (coupling unsafe)."
  negates:    "P4 (Ax_ψ_Preserve trust clause) in spirit — a large gap makes trust_AB ≥
               min(trust_A,trust_B) easy to satisfy numerically while the weak party is
               effectively governed by the strong one (capture risk, A0.1)."
  proof_sketch:
    "trust_axes.rs Def_TrustCompose clamps trust_parent ≤ min_child + ε. A gap larger than
     τ_threshold means the composed system's behavior is dominated by V_strong while
     V_weak's variety is under-weighted ⇒ asymmetric coupling can drive V_weak out of its
     R (one-sided contraction) ⇒ ¬viable(V_weak). This is a *capture* failure, not a
     dynamics failure — hence 'revisit handshake' (S5 re-consent) rather than hard-reject."
  enforcement:
    "coupling.rs Handshake bilateral consent + trust_axes scalar() feeding the
     TrustTriple; recommend τ_threshold default 0.2 (calibrate via EXP-TRUST-01)."


// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// ARBITER
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

definition(Def_ArbiterAPI):
  api:     "{ allocate(V_i, quota), report(V_i, usage), throttle(V_i, factor) }"
  pattern: "stateless function if N ≤ 2; a viable system V_arb (its own S1..S5) if N > 2
            or the topology is dynamic."
  invariants:
    "allocate enforces Cor_NoCompose_1 admission control (Σ quota ≤ B_h);
     throttle is the actuator when report(usage) shows a V_i exceeding its quota."


